# Rust
target/
Cargo.lock

# trunk / wasm-pack output
dist/
# ...but NOT the container2wasm boot glue, which only ever looked like build
# output. `dist/` matches at ANY depth, so this line silently swallowed
# web/c2w/dist/ too, and `runcontainer.js`, `stack-worker.js` and
# `worker-util.js` lived on ONE machine's disk while `publish.sh:56` gated on
# them and every deploy this project ever shipped copied them into gh-pages. A
# fresh clone could not pass gate check 6 (measured 2026-08-23:
# "GATE FAIL: Linux engine asset missing: dist/c2w/dist/runcontainer.js").
# They are upstream vendored files — `extras/runcontainerjs/dist`, checked in
# upstream (docs/IMAGE-RECIPE.md:277-278) — the exact siblings of
# web/c2w/vendor/, which was tracked all along. Negating the DIRECTORY is what
# works: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
!web/c2w/dist/
pkg/
node_modules/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Claude Code local state
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Legacy ASKK build artifacts kept on disk (recoverable only from gh-pages / slow rebuild)
out/
docs/bin/
docs/wasm/
.gstack/
__pycache__/

# --- the JavaScript tree ---
node_modules/
.next/
apps/web/out/
.deploy/
*.tsbuildinfo
